<title>GERMANY: Greenpeace plans gene-soy protest at Antwerp.</title>
<headline>Greenpeace plans gene-soy protest at Antwerp.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Environmental group Greenpeace is planning a protest action at the port of Antwerp to coincide with the arrival of the Polish freighter Zimia Zamoyska late on Thursday, activist Christine Kraemer said by telephone from Belgium.</p>
<p>She said the ship was carrying 18,000 tonnes of soybeans from Cleveland, Ohio, for processing by Cargill.</p>
<p>She said it was unclear whether or not the cargo included new crop soybeans that had been genetically modified.</p>
<p>Greenpeace is coordinating a campaign against the import of gene-altered soy, citing fears of possible health risks.</p>
<p>The beans, which were developed by U.S. chemicals group Monsanto to resist a weedkiller, have been given a clean bill of health in the U.S. and Europe.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
